Subject: [PATCH] arm: sequence scratch register allocation for doubleword shifts

Two gen_reg_rtx calls in one argument list have an unspecified evaluation
order. Native x86-64 and AArch64 compiler builds can number the resulting
pseudos differently even when preprocessed input and optimized GIMPLE match.
Allocate them in explicit statements before expanding the operation.

This affects ASHIFT, ASHIFTRT and LSHIFTRT. It changes only the order in which
scratch registers are allocated, not the shift semantics.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gcc/config/arm/arm.md | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/arm/arm.md b/gcc/config/arm/arm.md
--- a/gcc/config/arm/arm.md
+++ b/gcc/config/arm/arm.md
@@ -4620,5 +4620,6 @@
+  rtx scratch0 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
+  rtx scratch1 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
   arm_emit_coreregs_64bit_shift (ASHIFT, operands[0], operands[1],
-				 operands[2], gen_reg_rtx (SImode),
-				 gen_reg_rtx (SImode));
+				 operands[2], scratch0, scratch1);
   DONE;
 ")
@@ -4656,5 +4657,6 @@
+  rtx scratch0 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
+  rtx scratch1 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
   arm_emit_coreregs_64bit_shift (ASHIFTRT, operands[0], operands[1],
-				 operands[2], gen_reg_rtx (SImode),
-				 gen_reg_rtx (SImode));
+				 operands[2], scratch0, scratch1);
   DONE;
 ")
@@ -4688,5 +4690,6 @@
+  rtx scratch0 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
+  rtx scratch1 = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
   arm_emit_coreregs_64bit_shift (LSHIFTRT, operands[0], operands[1],
-				 operands[2], gen_reg_rtx (SImode),
-				 gen_reg_rtx (SImode));
+				 operands[2], scratch0, scratch1);
   DONE;
 ")
